@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core / cross-cutting. Core presentation/application/files or shared authority/recovery invariant remains applicable.
title Candidate concurrency model — independent bounded process workers
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

rectangle "Interactive admission\nCurrent actor / resource / versions" as I
rectangle "Background admission\nPolicy / quota / exact intent" as B
rectangle "Request-process capacity\nPer-operation isolated application context" as R
rectangle "Durable eligible work\nDuplicates possible; identity preserved" as Q
rectangle "Bounded job-process capacity\nAtomic claim / changing generation" as W
rectangle "Short owned transaction guards\nRequired per-resource ordering / optimistic versions" as T
rectangle "External operations\nNo SQL lock held during wait" as E
I --> R
B --> Q
Q --> W
R --> T
W --> T
W --> E
legend bottom
 Unrelated resources may progress concurrently within evaluated limits.
 Thread pools, event loops and actor models are alternatives, not simultaneously selected mechanisms.
 No worker count / timeout / mailbox / broker product is specified by this diagram.
endlegend
@enduml
